WEBVTT

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.820
<i>Am I going to die?</i>

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.680
<i>You're already dead.</i>

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:30.140
<i>Yes, long dead.</i>

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:32.540
<i>Who are you?</i>

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:43.320
Yuuko...

00:00:59.060 --> 00:01:03.620
The second we start, our bodies dive into the pool.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.050
All sound disappears.

00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:11.180
The gentle light shining through leaves me warm inside.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:16.640
If only I could stay like this, submerged for an eternity.

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.220
I don't like introducing myself.

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:52.580
Even if I were to do so,

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:57.310
it would just end up being about them, and the monster known as Inga.

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.420
Our fates are entwined beyond a shadow of doubt.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:05.720
I lost my family when I was a child.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.880
I grew up in the care of many people.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:14.200
They all said that so long as I grow up and help others,

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.950
it would be payment enough.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.530
Whenever I did well in swimming competitions,

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:30.380
my number of fans increased.

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:34.580
That's when I realized that gold medals were beyond my limits.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:39.020
I turned away from swimming and never looked back.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.400
It wouldn't help anyone after all.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:56.410
Then, a sudden realization came to me.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.940
It's so simple.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:02.550
I can help someone like this.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.810
I couldn't stop yet.

00:03:20.590 --> 00:03:23.810
I still haven't even helped anyone.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:27.930
It's a harsh reality we live in.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:32.610
That's why I wanted to give people hope through the fantasies that films beget.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:34.490
That's what I believed.

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:40.960
In time, I ran out of money.

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.100
Excuse me.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:10.570
You're from Japan, right?

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:13.450
I could use a hand.

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.120
Is the bill for gasoline separate?

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:27.120
Well, wouldn't that be nice?

00:04:27.770 --> 00:04:29.880
Whoa, that car's ancient!

00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.630
No way, it's you!

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:41.140
Everyone back home was worried sick, and you've been hiding out here?

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.760
Huh? The two of you know each other? How?

00:04:45.370 --> 00:04:47.900
I was on the same team as this punk in middle and high school.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:51.900
<i>I hadn't seen Serada Makiro since our high school graduation.</i>

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:55.650
<i>After his university graduation, he joined a travel agency.</i>

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:58.490
<i>He worked alongside Singing on the Battlefield,</i>

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:01.500
<i>a volunteer group that operated in troubled areas.</i>

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.460
It's such a relief to find someone familiar with the area.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.460
I'm Kurata Yuuko.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.220
Of course, they won't say it to my face.

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:22.700
But relatives, as well as others, believe Yuuko's group caused us to be forced into a war.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:29.490
Before the war, everyone called the four of them protective spirits of Japan.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:30.560
Wait.

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:33.530
Didn't Singing on the Battlefield have five members?

00:05:35.440 --> 00:05:36.280
Yuuko,

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:38.160
the leader, Saburi,

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:39.410
Yamaga,

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.660
Yasuda Kumi,

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.410
and Oono.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:46.290
Oono Myoushin was fine.

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:47.340
What?

00:05:54.140 --> 00:05:58.800
I... I wanted to see Hell!

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:04.310
Due to the killing of NPO volunteers,

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.810
the SDF have been ordered to dispatch.

00:06:07.390 --> 00:06:09.600
They said to avenge the civilians,

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.670
and that the government was in a weak position.

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:18.950
Oh, that's horrible.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:20.470
Do I really look like that?

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:25.540
Oh, he's here, Izzy.

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:40.190
Madam Koyama, who are they?

00:06:40.190 --> 00:06:44.230
They were recommended by Chairman Kaishou to assist in this investigation.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:48.460
This is Hayami from the Metropolitan Police Department. He'll provide you with the details.

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:55.360
A religious organization... called Bettenou?

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:01.720
It's been said that in this organization, established by Oono Myoushin,

00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:04.370
there have been people dying, one after another.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:19.260
Once a month, a ritual occurs in the
main shrine called the Dark Summoning.

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.010
The believers fall into a trance

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:29.320
while the Bettenou and self-proclaimed Leader Oono Myoushin judge their sins.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:37.280
Today, the sinners shall receive the judgment of the Dark Summoning.

00:08:07.810 --> 00:08:10.020
What is it?! Get me a clearer view!

00:08:18.590 --> 00:08:23.850
The deceased were believers whose families harbored doubts regarding the cult,

00:08:24.490 --> 00:08:31.620
but the beast couldn't be found, so the police didn't have a case for murder.

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:37.070
Did the undercover agent really see the beast?

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:41.710
He left the force and became a real believer.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.880
Oh, Great Leader!

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:53.680
Are the police are investigating the successive deaths?

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:56.230
The deceased's families are accusing you of being a scam cult!

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.020
That's the leader, Oono Myoushin.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:01.720
Oono...

00:09:13.970 --> 00:09:15.460
This is a holy place!

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:19.960
Oono Myoushin has shed blood for Japan's sake!

00:09:20.390 --> 00:09:22.210
He is a living god defending our country!

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:24.620
Isn't that the Self-Defense Force?

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.730
Public Security unit.

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:31.920
They're a legalized private security organization from a security firm, created as a part of the antiterrorism plan.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:35.080
They worship Oono like he's a god of war.

00:09:36.980 --> 00:09:38.270
What do you plan to do?

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:42.230
You said you wanted me to solve this case, right?

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:45.990
<i>That's not Oono.</i>

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:49.090
<i>Oono Myoushin is...</i>

00:09:50.230 --> 00:09:51.360
<i>dead.</i>

00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:12.550
What's this say?

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:15.700
Let me guess.

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:19.060
"Dreams will always come true," right?

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:21.870
Don't remember.

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.260
It's a great job isn't it?

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:25.440
The Traveling Cinema.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:30.990
You engage and excite children
who've never seen a film before.

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.900
Nowadays, no matter where you go,
you're connected by games.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:37.370
That is, unless your government bans it.

00:10:39.310 --> 00:10:40.780
What a waste...

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:50.340
Singing on the Battlefield, huh?

00:10:50.880 --> 00:10:53.040
I know what you want to say.

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:55.560
I've heard it enough times back home.

00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:58.320
They call it a publicity stunt, a death wish.

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:04.610
What could you possibly achieve by singing in strife-ridden lands?

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:09.050
Sure, we can't really sing <i>on</i> the battlefield...

00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:13.410
but we <i>can</i> bring a smile to the faces of children worn out by the fighting.

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:16.340
So, that feeling of satisfaction is your reward.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:21.870
The children laugh because you're ridiculous.

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:24.630
The candy probably helps.

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:29.050
After all, even you don't really think this makes anything better.

00:11:29.700 --> 00:11:34.140
You guys just don't want to admit how insignificant your existence is.

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:48.380
Pot calling the kettle black?

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:53.760
My family runs a shrine, so if you have any troubles, come to me.

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:55.280
It's ok.

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:56.910
Go on, Yuuko.

00:12:10.750 --> 00:12:13.310
The anti-government rebels have already started moving.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:15.210
Do you really intend to guide them around?

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:17.890
We have a lot of catching up to do.

00:12:18.280 --> 00:12:20.040
So let's not talk about that.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.890
Still swimming?

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:35.730
Against the raging tides of life, or something like that?

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:37.640
Just 'cause we were on the swim team.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:40.670
You can't live off just swimming.

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:44.040
If it were up to me, I'd swim even for horrible pay.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:59.970
Ah, why do I have to grow up?

00:13:01.730 --> 00:13:04.170
It's about time you ended your soul-searching trip, isn't it?

00:13:04.170 --> 00:13:08.800
Don't summarize my life with such cheap words.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:11.980
But those <i>cheap words</i> sum it up exactly.

00:13:12.590 --> 00:13:13.620
I...

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:16.580
still haven't done it.

00:13:35.410 --> 00:13:37.470
Aren't you afraid to be alone?

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:40.550
No need to watch me.

00:13:40.550 --> 00:13:41.970
I'm not going anywhere.

00:13:46.250 --> 00:13:47.090
Ouch.

00:13:55.220 --> 00:13:56.360
Can I have this?

00:14:04.370 --> 00:14:10.660
<i>The next day we entered an area where the battle against anti-government rebels aided by the UN intensified.</i>

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:14.120
Are you sure you'll be fine with one hand?

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:16.260
Hey, I just washed that.

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:20.890
Oh yeah, that's why we're here.

00:14:22.710 --> 00:14:23.510
What's that sound?

00:14:24.870 --> 00:14:26.270
Sounds like a QW.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:27.680
An RPG?

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:29.060
No way!

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:33.790
Did you see that?!

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:35.940
Are they trying to kill us?!

00:14:53.550 --> 00:14:55.090
Everyone out! Now!

00:15:22.070 --> 00:15:22.910
Yuuko...

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:43.510
There aren't enough souls!

00:15:45.950 --> 00:15:47.640
That's strange.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:51.080
Oono Myoushin said that apart from us, no one could enter,

00:15:51.080 --> 00:15:52.560
and he's right.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:59.500
Oh, you were the inside man, right?

00:15:59.500 --> 00:16:01.390
Unfortunately, yes.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:05.250
Now, I do not have the slightest doubt about Bettenou.

00:16:05.250 --> 00:16:07.270
I know where you're coming from.

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:09.270
That Hayami sure is weird.

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:11.650
I don't really like him.

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:14.210
I was in the same department.

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:19.350
By the way, what were you doing with those two earlier?

00:16:19.350 --> 00:16:22.220
Getting those calls and stuff...

00:16:22.910 --> 00:16:26.010
The leader's words will definitely come true.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:30.390
Bettenou is a living god.

00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:36.100
It's been a while.

00:16:36.750 --> 00:16:39.020
I didn't think you were still alive.

00:16:43.140 --> 00:16:46.160
How long are you going to keep up this farce,

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:47.160
Serada?!

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:52.440
Serada, help us!

00:16:54.020 --> 00:16:56.080
There's something wrong with this guy!

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:58.120
Serada, where are you?

00:16:58.770 --> 00:17:00.930
Oh shit. Oh, holy shit!

00:17:05.210 --> 00:17:06.720
Serada?

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:08.550
You think I'm that travel agent?

00:17:09.080 --> 00:17:12.310
The only possible survivor was Serada.

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:17.560
I am Oono Myoushin.

00:17:30.410 --> 00:17:31.620
Oono.

00:17:31.620 --> 00:17:35.210
The leader is only covering his scars. How dare you?!

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:41.100
This x-ray is of Oono Myoushin before he left Japan,

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:43.000
and this is him after he returned.

00:17:43.920 --> 00:17:50.140
We couldn't be sure it was him by his facial structure, so he suggested this comparison.

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:53.390
You think they're the same? <i>These</i> two shots?

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:55.990
It's as it seems.

00:18:02.170 --> 00:18:06.250
Oono Myoushin released this video after returning.

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:08.420
As you can see,

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:14.790
the Singing on the Battlefield members are captured by government troops and tortured.

00:18:15.430 --> 00:18:18.480
The scene changes to those four getting executed.

00:18:20.100 --> 00:18:21.970
Izzy, was it?

00:18:21.970 --> 00:18:23.130
Koyama!

00:18:23.690 --> 00:18:26.550
You can see that video?

00:18:26.550 --> 00:18:27.820
Yes.

00:18:31.600 --> 00:18:34.320
The government banned the video,

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:37.220
but through online distribution systems like the JJ Systems, the video spread,

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:40.060
and public opinion for the dispatch of the SDF solidified.

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:44.110
But people who returned after the war, as well as a number of foreigners,

00:18:44.110 --> 00:18:48.190
pointed out that this video shows no such scenes.

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:52.280
That the video is only of the sky and noise.

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:56.350
It <i>is</i> the sky though, isn't it?

00:18:56.350 --> 00:18:57.330
Yep, it's the sky.

00:18:57.330 --> 00:19:01.010
But we can see it clearly!

00:19:01.010 --> 00:19:04.370
The four youths are being shot in cold-blood.

00:19:05.970 --> 00:19:09.680
Some can see the video, and some can't?

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:11.750
How is that even possible?!

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:14.330
Answer me! You must know something!

00:19:15.460 --> 00:19:18.310
What do you know about me, Izzy?

00:19:20.630 --> 00:19:22.810
I don't know anything...

00:19:23.250 --> 00:19:28.000
but Chairman Kaishou said that you were together with Oono and the others.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:28.930
Kaishou?

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.450
Chairman of JJ Systems,

00:19:33.010 --> 00:19:35.200
and special advisor to the Public Prosecutors office.

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:42.100
You ate Oono.

00:19:42.870 --> 00:19:44.610
Not only Oono,

00:19:44.610 --> 00:19:47.470
but Kumi, Saburi, Yamaga...

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.350
and Yuuko.

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:00.680
Serada!

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:02.420
Serada!

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:03.330
Shut up!

00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:06.770
We're both being watched.

00:20:10.700 --> 00:20:14.110
Where have you been the entire time?

00:20:15.040 --> 00:20:19.060
I've been watching Oono Myoushin.

00:20:19.610 --> 00:20:21.960
Is that really Oono?

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:24.900
I plan to speak to him tonight,

00:20:25.440 --> 00:20:27.730
but he has a strange power.

00:20:28.290 --> 00:20:31.530
I want you and your friend to accompany me.

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:36.390
All right.

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:39.110
I'll explain everything then.

00:20:54.290 --> 00:20:55.410
Am I going to die?

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:58.120
<i>You're already dead.</i>

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:10.440
<i>Did you do this?</i>

00:21:11.330 --> 00:21:13.000
<i>What are you?</i>

00:21:14.170 --> 00:21:15.010
Inga.

00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:20.390
<i>You humans gave me that name.</i>

00:21:23.230 --> 00:21:26.140
It's been a while since I've eaten souls.

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:28.520
You're... alive?

00:21:29.090 --> 00:21:31.400
Hey, you were stabbed through the neck, weren't you?

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:34.240
What the hell are you?!

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:36.450
Where's Serada?

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:38.450
He was here when we crashed, wasn't he?

00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:39.990
Serada, help us!

00:21:40.320 --> 00:21:43.340
<i>Did Serada get caught in the explosion?</i>

00:21:40.640 --> 00:21:42.540
There's something wrong with this guy!

00:21:44.260 --> 00:21:44.910
Souls!

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:47.630
Each and every one of you is so big!

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:52.050
You're disgusting!

00:21:56.320 --> 00:21:57.870
What are you going to do?

00:21:57.870 --> 00:21:59.010
I'm not scared at all!

00:21:59.470 --> 00:22:01.460
I don't care when I die!

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:12.050
I know.

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:15.690
No one really listens to my songs.

00:22:16.530 --> 00:22:18.320
Even if I sing here,

00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:20.200
it won't bring anyone happiness.

00:22:20.530 --> 00:22:22.400
I'll forget...

00:22:23.380 --> 00:22:24.830
everything I didn't want to hear!

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:35.430
You can eat other stuff than souls?

00:22:35.430 --> 00:22:39.300
Have you forgotten that I have a human body?

00:22:40.110 --> 00:22:44.400
Is the soul the hidden truth in a person's heart?

00:22:44.400 --> 00:22:45.810
It's their screams.

00:22:46.420 --> 00:22:47.540
Screams?

00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:50.570
Living organisms have their own unique traits.

00:22:50.570 --> 00:22:55.110
For example, a certain kind of ant produces a honey-like substance in their bodies.

00:22:55.110 --> 00:22:57.390
Camels store water in their humps too.

00:22:57.390 --> 00:22:58.880
Actually, it's not water.

00:22:58.880 --> 00:22:59.700
Really?

00:23:01.380 --> 00:23:03.450
Well, humans store screams.

00:23:10.730 --> 00:23:13.520
If I change myself, the world will change too.

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:17.840
My thoughts become the power to change the world.

00:23:18.240 --> 00:23:20.540
That's nonsense.

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:23.090
I don't want to change!

00:23:23.090 --> 00:23:25.720
I-I'm fine the way I am!

00:23:26.160 --> 00:23:27.810
Don't change me!

00:23:31.710 --> 00:23:35.130
Why is it only him that makes ridiculous amounts of money?

00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:37.360
How long will I stay poor?

00:23:37.700 --> 00:23:40.890
There's no reason for me not to be rich.

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:42.890
Pay more attention to me!

00:23:42.890 --> 00:23:44.570
Listen to me more!

00:23:44.570 --> 00:23:46.200
Praise me more!

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:46.870
Praise me!

00:23:46.870 --> 00:23:47.910
Praise me!

00:23:57.690 --> 00:24:01.300
Do I have screams inside of me as well?

00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:03.190
Don't you understand?

00:24:03.790 --> 00:24:06.550
Humans sure are absurd.

00:24:10.050 --> 00:24:12.440
<i>I thought I understood.</i>

00:24:13.620 --> 00:24:16.020
I wanted to be able to help others.

00:24:16.390 --> 00:24:19.420
<i>But it was just wishful thinking.</i>

00:24:20.190 --> 00:24:23.610
<i>What did the real me want to do?</i>

00:24:23.610 --> 00:24:25.430
<i>What did I wish for?</i>

00:24:26.320 --> 00:24:28.410
I'll tell you last.

00:24:29.670 --> 00:24:33.020
Okay, then let's end it.

00:24:35.120 --> 00:24:36.980
Wait a moment! You—

00:24:52.880 --> 00:24:56.480
I... I wanted to see Hell.

00:24:57.060 --> 00:24:58.990
I wanted to see people killing each other,

00:24:58.990 --> 00:25:00.980
and the hell known as the battlefield.

00:25:01.350 --> 00:25:04.990
I wanted to see proof that there is no God and no Buddha.

00:25:18.820 --> 00:25:20.570
You police should fall back!

00:25:20.570 --> 00:25:23.480
We know that the criminal who
murdered Leader Oono Myoushin

00:25:23.480 --> 00:25:25.980
is affiliated with the police!

00:25:25.980 --> 00:25:27.890
You guys murdered him!

00:25:30.110 --> 00:25:31.780
Oono's dead?

00:25:31.780 --> 00:25:32.770
Serada...

00:25:33.580 --> 00:25:35.060
Don't move! Raise your hands!

00:25:35.510 --> 00:25:37.690
Why did you kill Oono, you bastard?!

00:25:37.690 --> 00:25:41.150
It was already over by the time I arrived.

00:25:41.670 --> 00:25:43.530
How could I have killed him?

00:25:43.990 --> 00:25:45.150
I saw it with my own eyes!

00:25:55.990 --> 00:25:58.830
You were even caught on camera!

00:26:00.300 --> 00:26:02.380
There he is! The guy from this afternoon!

00:26:02.930 --> 00:26:04.630
The police were hiding him, huh?!

00:26:15.420 --> 00:26:16.610
That wasn't Oono.

00:26:16.610 --> 00:26:17.560
Impossible!

00:26:20.640 --> 00:26:21.230
Arrest him!

00:26:32.210 --> 00:26:34.210
Over here!

00:26:34.210 --> 00:26:34.910
Get him!

00:26:44.320 --> 00:26:47.170
Why did it turn out like this?

00:26:47.910 --> 00:26:51.920
You people are always lying to yourselves.

00:26:52.810 --> 00:26:57.060
For every lie, your soul gets riper.

00:27:02.570 --> 00:27:06.760
Please, let me sing for the sake of the children.

00:27:06.760 --> 00:27:09.330
That's not what your soul says.

00:27:09.330 --> 00:27:10.570
Let me show you.

00:27:14.880 --> 00:27:18.770
Ah, why?

00:27:18.770 --> 00:27:23.630
Why do I grow up?

00:27:40.060 --> 00:27:41.350
Hey, that hurts.

00:27:54.160 --> 00:27:56.730
If we can't figure it out by morning,

00:27:56.730 --> 00:27:59.370
Chairman Kaishou will denounce you as the perpetrator.

00:28:01.390 --> 00:28:03.830
This place is pretty rundown, huh?

00:28:03.830 --> 00:28:08.980
This is the first area hit by terrorists when the SDF ramped up their operations in the troubled area.

00:28:23.050 --> 00:28:25.530
I investigated Serada Makiro.

00:28:28.510 --> 00:28:29.110
Oh?

00:28:30.430 --> 00:28:31.860
The SDF?

00:28:32.260 --> 00:28:34.420
He was an excellent officer candidate,

00:28:34.420 --> 00:28:36.150
though this was when he was still in the SDF.

00:28:36.150 --> 00:28:37.170
Was?

00:28:37.170 --> 00:28:41.250
Before the war, he died in a traffic accident.

00:28:42.260 --> 00:28:46.800
That's why he couldn't possibly be a travel agent overseas.

00:28:54.080 --> 00:28:57.410
Suddenly bombers appear in the sky,

00:28:57.410 --> 00:29:00.310
and artillery fire can be heard.

00:29:00.310 --> 00:29:03.140
It's war. Another war has started.

00:29:30.400 --> 00:29:32.720
This is impossible!

00:29:43.510 --> 00:29:44.370
Yo.

00:29:44.370 --> 00:29:45.040
Yo.

00:29:45.970 --> 00:29:47.240
Don't worry.

00:29:47.860 --> 00:29:49.900
Until we're done talking, this place is safe.

00:29:56.330 --> 00:29:59.230
This one here was in the same place as that boy.

00:30:20.940 --> 00:30:24.060
It's the power of words, isn't it?

00:30:24.770 --> 00:30:25.770
It turns your words...

00:30:25.770 --> 00:30:27.690
Into reality.

00:30:28.650 --> 00:30:31.590
Did you know them?

00:30:31.590 --> 00:30:33.190
Not really.

00:30:33.190 --> 00:30:35.020
Originally, my mission...

00:30:35.020 --> 00:30:37.900
Oh, you do know it was a mission, don't you?

00:30:37.900 --> 00:30:39.290
SDF...

00:30:39.290 --> 00:30:42.260
Or rather, a faction of the SDF.

00:30:42.260 --> 00:30:46.320
I was to take some NPO volunteers into a dangerous area and be attacked.

00:30:46.320 --> 00:30:51.670
It would've been okay for the van to just be shot at, but to be completely wiped out...

00:30:52.170 --> 00:30:54.980
And I met this by coincidence.

00:30:54.980 --> 00:30:56.730
Actually, it was fate.

00:30:57.980 --> 00:31:01.300
Did you know that this is a god?

00:31:01.640 --> 00:31:02.550
A god?

00:31:03.950 --> 00:31:08.080
Long, long ago, this country sent soldiers overseas.

00:31:08.080 --> 00:31:11.880
Not only soldiers, but also gods to protect the soldiers.

00:31:13.140 --> 00:31:14.690
Should they die,

00:31:14.690 --> 00:31:18.670
the gods wouldn't be able to return home and were left where they lay...

00:31:18.670 --> 00:31:19.820
forever.

00:31:21.570 --> 00:31:23.420
You believe that?

00:31:23.420 --> 00:31:25.030
Did you forget?

00:31:25.030 --> 00:31:27.830
My words turn into reality.

00:31:27.830 --> 00:31:30.420
It already <i>is</i> the truth.

00:31:30.420 --> 00:31:34.230
You returned as Oono Myoushin.

00:31:34.230 --> 00:31:35.960
If you say you're Oono,

00:31:35.960 --> 00:31:37.960
then even the eyes of a doctor will be deceived.

00:31:38.490 --> 00:31:41.770
If you say it's a video of four people being executed,

00:31:41.770 --> 00:31:44.970
then even a mere scenic video becomes a shocking one.

00:31:46.790 --> 00:31:49.180
Why did you impersonate Oono?

00:31:49.180 --> 00:31:51.940
Because I didn't want this child taken away from me.

00:31:51.940 --> 00:31:55.700
So you founded a religious sect to suck money from your believers,

00:31:55.700 --> 00:31:57.980
and snuffed out any who wanted to leave?

00:31:58.390 --> 00:32:02.500
All I did was say that unbelievers would be judged.

00:32:02.500 --> 00:32:03.560
Why?

00:32:03.560 --> 00:32:06.870
If you have the power of God,
why squander it on acts like that?

00:32:06.870 --> 00:32:09.020
Isn't there something else you could do?

00:32:09.020 --> 00:32:11.250
Like help people?

00:32:13.100 --> 00:32:14.480
And what would that entail?

00:32:14.480 --> 00:32:16.840
To rid the world of war?

00:32:17.280 --> 00:32:21.790
To give homes to people who've lost their own?

00:32:22.350 --> 00:32:27.600
Those who did not receive a home would cry foul, and claim unfairness.

00:32:27.600 --> 00:32:30.040
Is it god's duty to save these people?

00:32:30.040 --> 00:32:32.390
I won't fancify it like you.

00:32:33.490 --> 00:32:38.650
In the pool, I only wished for my own victory in this world.

00:32:45.600 --> 00:32:48.370
If you stand, I will disappear.

00:32:48.370 --> 00:32:50.120
Why did you make me the perpetrator?

00:32:58.760 --> 00:33:01.050
The war has ended.

00:33:08.520 --> 00:33:11.520
Inga, are you guys gods?

00:33:12.060 --> 00:33:15.650
I forgot to tell you, but that one's a dud.

00:33:16.500 --> 00:33:19.230
The soldiers that left this country in the past

00:33:19.230 --> 00:33:21.530
fell in another land and left behind their regrets.

00:33:21.940 --> 00:33:24.830
Their regrets amalgamated to form a demon.

00:33:24.830 --> 00:33:28.720
The demon that Bettenou sealed is this boy.

00:33:31.440 --> 00:33:35.460
To ye that awakened the demon, let God's judgment fall upon ye.

00:33:40.480 --> 00:33:41.840
That's the beast from the Dark Summoning?!

00:33:53.760 --> 00:33:55.140
It's useless.

00:33:55.140 --> 00:33:58.480
You, who haven't even fully awakened, can't hope to touch Bettenou.

00:34:04.880 --> 00:34:12.100
When will I grow up into an adult, I wonder?

00:34:15.980 --> 00:34:17.980
What are you doing, Yuuko?

00:34:37.530 --> 00:34:40.690
You did this to free me?

00:34:45.000 --> 00:34:47.110
My soul, was it?

00:34:47.110 --> 00:34:51.200
I just didn't want anyone to see it.

00:34:52.470 --> 00:34:53.920
Which do you think it is?

00:34:55.530 --> 00:34:59.650
Nobody ever truly says what they feel.

00:35:00.270 --> 00:35:03.590
But that's not the only truth,

00:35:04.250 --> 00:35:06.830
People have many sides to their heart.

00:35:07.390 --> 00:35:09.590
They're all truths.

00:35:10.620 --> 00:35:14.850
You will not decide mine!

00:35:30.480 --> 00:35:33.240
Damn, I missed out on her soul.

00:35:34.980 --> 00:35:36.920
Inga, is that you?

00:35:36.920 --> 00:35:38.610
She's dead.

00:35:38.610 --> 00:35:43.720
If she was only halfway there like you,
I could've brought her back.

00:35:46.460 --> 00:35:49.630
What if I were to do the same?

00:35:49.940 --> 00:35:51.460
You'd rather die?

00:35:51.460 --> 00:35:52.250
No way!

00:35:52.250 --> 00:35:56.010
Why did you revive me and steal my body?

00:35:56.010 --> 00:35:57.770
Why not kill me like the others?

00:35:59.410 --> 00:36:00.770
Your blood...

00:36:01.650 --> 00:36:05.240
So you're incomplete.

00:36:06.010 --> 00:36:10.640
You revived me because you still need my blood.

00:36:14.630 --> 00:36:16.320
Let's strike a deal.

00:36:16.320 --> 00:36:17.160
A deal?

00:36:18.090 --> 00:36:20.530
Never steal my body again.

00:36:21.480 --> 00:36:24.020
If you eat someone's scream you won't take their life.

00:36:25.270 --> 00:36:28.750
If you were able to revive me, then you should be able to do that much.

00:36:30.020 --> 00:36:33.060
And in return?

00:36:33.060 --> 00:36:34.620
Souls.

00:36:34.620 --> 00:36:35.430
How many?

00:36:36.220 --> 00:36:37.730
Any number of them.

00:36:39.440 --> 00:36:41.810
I'll tell you where the best place would be to get them.

00:36:42.740 --> 00:36:45.930
I know where there are many screams,

00:36:45.930 --> 00:36:48.830
locked away in people's hearts,

00:36:49.480 --> 00:36:51.040
taken to the grave.

00:36:53.540 --> 00:36:55.450
What do you get out of this?

00:36:55.960 --> 00:36:58.680
Tell me about my soul one day.

00:36:59.500 --> 00:37:01.830
Tell me what I really wish for.

00:37:04.320 --> 00:37:05.720
I accept.

00:37:05.720 --> 00:37:07.810
And don't take that form.

00:37:15.900 --> 00:37:16.770
What's this?

00:37:21.690 --> 00:37:23.640
I can't do shit to this thing!

00:37:24.080 --> 00:37:26.650
Fangs rip through the chest, fresh blood surging forth.

00:37:29.350 --> 00:37:30.230
Inga.

00:37:31.200 --> 00:37:34.360
How do you eat a soul without taking a life?

00:37:35.120 --> 00:37:36.180
What are you saying?

00:37:36.180 --> 00:37:36.740
Answer me!

00:37:38.000 --> 00:37:38.990
A question!

00:37:39.480 --> 00:37:46.000
If you can ask a question that opens their soul,
then they'll honestly answer that single question.

00:37:46.680 --> 00:37:48.050
Great.

00:37:48.050 --> 00:37:54.260
Ask me what I see with my own two eyes!

00:37:54.260 --> 00:37:56.580
That goes against the deal!

00:37:56.580 --> 00:37:59.820
Didn't you want to know what you truly wanted?

00:38:00.570 --> 00:38:04.930
I won't let the likes of you decide what's true for me.

00:38:06.010 --> 00:38:07.310
Ask me, Inga!

00:38:08.750 --> 00:38:12.320
Okay, but I'll turn into that form.

00:38:23.700 --> 00:38:24.830
Demon.

00:38:40.550 --> 00:38:41.350
Tell me,

00:38:42.690 --> 00:38:46.350
What do you see with your own two eyes?

00:38:48.360 --> 00:38:49.480
What do you see?

00:38:55.000 --> 00:38:55.940
Rain,

00:38:57.070 --> 00:38:58.030
and Yuuko.

00:38:59.280 --> 00:39:00.240
Only you!

00:39:20.290 --> 00:39:22.510
There aren't any bombers or tanks.

00:39:23.150 --> 00:39:24.300
That beast does not exist.

00:39:27.810 --> 00:39:30.070
He shouldn't be able to see me.

00:39:30.970 --> 00:39:33.190
My words are reality.

00:39:33.680 --> 00:39:35.790
That's the power of Bettenou.

00:39:36.880 --> 00:39:40.010
It creates an illusion, making it seem as if your words were reality.

00:39:40.730 --> 00:39:42.720
If you say so,

00:39:42.720 --> 00:39:44.570
then you'll see what isn't actually there.

00:39:45.070 --> 00:39:48.100
That's why among those that watched the video,

00:39:48.100 --> 00:39:50.330
there were people who couldn't see the execution.

00:39:50.710 --> 00:39:53.710
Like me, they did not hear your words.

00:39:54.200 --> 00:39:55.930
What you see is reality.

00:39:56.590 --> 00:39:58.550
My words change reality!

00:39:58.910 --> 00:40:01.870
Even if you were to delude the brain,

00:40:02.440 --> 00:40:04.430
my soul sees the truth.

00:40:06.260 --> 00:40:11.060
The illusion of a beast caused your believers to rend their own flesh.

00:40:11.950 --> 00:40:13.940
Now, your illusion won't last.

00:40:15.910 --> 00:40:17.320
Is this an illusion, too?

00:40:19.540 --> 00:40:20.110
Don't move!

00:40:21.020 --> 00:40:21.860
I said don't move!

00:40:22.530 --> 00:40:26.070
Oono Myoushin, you're the suspect for the murders of your believers.

00:40:26.410 --> 00:40:27.580
Your perpetrator is right here.

00:40:28.680 --> 00:40:32.210
The true perpetrator is shot and killed by the police!

00:40:50.430 --> 00:40:52.320
Impossible!

00:40:53.450 --> 00:40:54.560
Why?

00:40:54.990 --> 00:40:55.770
Bettenou.

00:40:58.510 --> 00:41:00.020
You said so yourself.

00:41:00.630 --> 00:41:03.150
"The true perpetrator is shot and killed."

00:41:16.240 --> 00:41:19.950
I thought I had God in my hands.

00:41:20.850 --> 00:41:25.880
Did you know that love is the same as God?

00:41:33.740 --> 00:41:35.320
It was as you said.

00:41:35.320 --> 00:41:38.680
The DNA analysis of the corpse assumed to be Oono Myoushin

00:41:38.680 --> 00:41:42.400
came back positive for former undercover agent, Makita.

00:41:43.220 --> 00:41:46.280
He made Makita pretend to be Oono, then killed him.

00:41:51.690 --> 00:41:53.100
And you are?

00:41:55.490 --> 00:41:57.170
I have Chairman Kaishou on the phone for you.

00:41:59.430 --> 00:42:00.790
Kaishou Rinroku here.

00:42:01.210 --> 00:42:02.530
What do you want?

00:42:02.530 --> 00:42:06.360
As planned, it will be reported with you as the main perpetrator.

00:42:06.360 --> 00:42:08.970
What? Wai—What do y—

00:42:10.390 --> 00:42:13.210
Serada Makiro has already been pronounced dead.

00:42:14.020 --> 00:42:17.950
You, who have just returned, committed the crimes.

00:42:17.950 --> 00:42:19.950
That is my reasoning.

00:42:19.950 --> 00:42:21.440
What reasoning?

00:42:21.440 --> 00:42:22.460
That's a load of bullshit!

00:42:22.460 --> 00:42:25.400
Would you rather I laid everything out for the world to see?

00:42:25.400 --> 00:42:29.950
Want me to tell them how Oono Myoushin, Kurata Yuuko, and the others died?

00:42:31.200 --> 00:42:33.810
What do you know?

00:42:33.810 --> 00:42:34.980
About what?

00:42:34.980 --> 00:42:40.380
Serada said that he received a mission from some faction to lead the NPO volunteers in a troubled area.

00:42:41.060 --> 00:42:43.880
It was to pull this country into war.

00:42:44.330 --> 00:42:48.130
My, my. You're a bit childish to pull out such a conspiracy theory.

00:42:48.130 --> 00:42:52.590
I will not forgive those that use Yuuko and the others' deaths for their own gains.

00:42:53.190 --> 00:42:56.040
They're not some fine sacrifice.

00:43:02.140 --> 00:43:04.420
This is your new name.

00:43:04.420 --> 00:43:07.820
You were shot and killed as an accused murderer.

00:43:08.570 --> 00:43:10.450
Having no identity would be a problem, right?

00:43:11.090 --> 00:43:13.640
You wouldn't even be able to rent videos.

00:43:13.640 --> 00:43:15.200
Is that so?

00:43:15.710 --> 00:43:17.600
Your real identity,

00:43:17.600 --> 00:43:19.910
which has been involved in terrorism,

00:43:19.910 --> 00:43:21.710
will disappear with Chairman Kaishou's efforts.

00:43:22.160 --> 00:43:23.360
You should be thankful.

00:43:32.550 --> 00:43:34.950
Where are you going? I can give you a ride.

00:43:34.950 --> 00:43:36.470
I'm going to live here.

00:43:36.470 --> 00:43:40.100
It's off limits and no one would ever live here, right?

00:43:47.660 --> 00:43:48.930
What happened to the girl?

00:43:48.930 --> 00:43:50.300
The girl?

00:43:50.300 --> 00:43:51.750
The god.

00:43:51.750 --> 00:43:53.440
She's your acquaintance, right?

00:43:53.440 --> 00:43:56.400
She went off somewhere, and she's not an acquaintance.

00:43:57.120 --> 00:43:59.120
Would you have preferred her over me?

00:43:57.790 --> 00:44:01.580
I whisper my prayers

00:44:00.730 --> 00:44:04.490
I'd rather choose a demon over a god who's nothing but words.

00:44:01.580 --> 00:44:05.540
to the haze of dawn

00:44:05.000 --> 00:44:08.510
Now you'll never know what you truly want.

00:44:05.750 --> 00:44:09.310
With our fingers

00:44:09.180 --> 00:44:11.780
Even so, you won't be able to get away from me.

00:44:09.730 --> 00:44:13.800
we trace a twisted landscape

00:44:11.780 --> 00:44:13.160
I know.

00:44:13.160 --> 00:44:15.200
I'll keep feeding you souls.

00:44:13.800 --> 00:44:17.810
We look for truth,

00:44:16.450 --> 00:44:18.640
This world is crawling with liars.

00:44:17.810 --> 00:44:21.760
so we'd never settle for lies

00:44:21.760 --> 00:44:26.650
To know each other perfectly, eventually,

00:44:23.820 --> 00:44:26.650
Yuuki Shinjurou, huh?

00:44:27.920 --> 00:44:29.800
we walk this road

00:44:29.800 --> 00:44:33.830
I try to surpass words

00:44:33.830 --> 00:44:37.720
and fail like falling feathers

00:44:37.720 --> 00:44:41.280
I try to find something

00:44:41.710 --> 00:44:47.490
so that we can be together here

00:44:53.800 --> 00:44:57.840
I try to find something to put my days in order

00:44:57.840 --> 00:45:02.010
like scattered clouds

00:45:02.010 --> 00:45:04.870
I try to find something

00:45:05.990 --> 00:45:10.930
so that we can be together here

00:45:25.560 --> 00:45:29.670
Together we look for a reason,

00:45:29.670 --> 00:45:33.720
yet tell our stories alone

00:45:33.720 --> 00:45:37.660
I keep peeling off my scabs,

00:45:37.660 --> 00:45:40.260
unable to heal

00:45:40.000 --> 00:45:41.720
unable to heal

00:45:41.720 --> 00:45:45.650
Saying that false beauty is good enough

00:45:45.650 --> 00:45:49.690
is not acceptable

00:45:49.690 --> 00:45:54.530
To forgive  each other

00:45:55.970 --> 00:45:57.710
we walk this road

00:45:57.710 --> 00:46:01.680
I try to find hands held out to me

00:46:01.680 --> 00:46:05.710
like waves upon the shore

00:46:05.710 --> 00:46:08.870
I try to find something

00:46:09.730 --> 00:46:15.860
so that we can be together here

00:46:35.690 --> 00:46:40.190
This can't be happening; I clasp my head in my hands

00:46:40.190 --> 00:46:46.780
As I struggle with my desire to escape from this saturated world.

00:46:47.620 --> 00:46:52.210
Time goes flowing past with the rustling roar of sand.

00:46:52.210 --> 00:46:55.630
Things never get any better.

00:46:55.630 --> 00:46:58.550
I'm gazing on toward a dreamless tomorrow.

00:47:00.340 --> 00:47:05.840
I want to bid farewell to my days of constantly feeling lost.

00:47:06.850 --> 00:47:11.310
I try stretching out my hand in resistance.

00:47:11.310 --> 00:47:17.060
We'll cry millions upon millions of tears, then be reborn.

00:47:17.060 --> 00:47:23.200
Let's keep going, with red in our eyes, toward the future we drew for ourselves.

00:47:23.200 --> 00:47:28.950
Come over to me; I'm clapping my hands.

00:47:28.950 --> 00:47:30.910
Who are you? Where are you coming from?

00:47:30.910 --> 00:47:35.250
I strain my eyes in the darkness.

00:47:35.250 --> 00:47:40.840
I can't see a thing, and nothing makes sense, but I'll go anyway.

00:47:40.840 --> 00:47:47.340
To the place where you're waiting, lit by a beacon of light.

00:47:47.350 --> 00:47:50.350
Inspired by Ango Sakaguchi's Meiji-era Detective Stories:
"The Wonders of Evil Teachings" and "The Demobilized Killer Affair"

00:47:52.600 --> 00:47:55.180
A phone call this early in the morning?

00:47:55.180 --> 00:47:57.590
Ah. Thanks, Rie.

00:47:57.590 --> 00:47:59.430
Pulling an all-nighter is tough.

00:47:59.430 --> 00:48:02.610
It's 'cause everyone keeps only asking you for advice.

00:48:03.420 --> 00:48:04.490
Who's this?

00:48:03.660 --> 00:48:05.240
Daughter of Kaishou Rinroku, student

00:48:03.660 --> 00:48:05.240
Chairman of Japan Justice Network System Holdings

00:48:04.490 --> 00:48:06.990
Oh, interested?

00:48:06.990 --> 00:48:10.190
Not at all! He's not my type.
